.SH FILE ACTIONS
.B lcp [PATH]
;
.B lmv [PATH]
;
.B lscp [PATH]
;
.B lrm [PATH]
.
.TP
.B lmk FILE.ext
Create an empty file through LOOK's undo journal.
.TP
.B lmk DIR/
Create a directory and enter it. The creation is journaled for
.B lk undo
.
.TP
.B lmk -f NAME
Force file creation when the name is ambiguous.
.TP
.B lmk -d NAME
Force directory creation and enter it.
.TP
.B mkd DIR
Compatibility wrapper for
.B lmk -d DIR
.
.PP
A trailing slash is directory intent. Names with a filename suffix and dotfiles imply file intent.
Extensionless names are prompted as directory or file. The choice is accepted immediately from a single key; Return is not required.
Missing parent directories for file creation require confirmation.
Undo removes only an unchanged empty created file or an empty created directory.
.SH SHORTCUTS
l/ls smart view; ll details; ld directories; lf files; lt tree; lr recent; lz sizes;
zll fuzzy jump + look; cdl jump + details; f find anywhere; lh home; lo Ollama chat;
rs reset ritual; rb reload zsh; webterm terminal over Tailscale.
.SH CAPABILITY MODEL
Remote inference and local authority are separate:
.B lo @HOST --power
runs inference on HOST while commands execute on the computer running LOOK.
Thinking-capable output is visually separated into
.B thinking >
and
.B lo >
sections; tool activity remains distinct.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/look/look.zsh
.br
.I ~/.zsh_secrets
.br
.I ~/.config/look/

.SH COMPLETION
LOOK installs context-sensitive Zsh completion for
.B lk
and
.B lo
under ~/.config/look/completions.
Commands such as
.B lk ollama
,
.B lk memory
, and
.B lk skills
complete their valid subcommands. The
.B lmk
completion exposes file/directory force flags and existing parent directories.
Saved Ollama host names are completed dynamically.
LO completion stops at its command/options layer so free-form prompt text remains free-form.
.SH VERSION SAFETY
Future Crash + LOOK installers write a versioned install manifest under
~/.local/share/look/install_manifest.json.
A current installer refuses to overwrite a newer unified release unless
.B --force-downgrade
is supplied deliberately.
Historical installers predating this guard cannot be retroactively protected.

.SH MEDIA
.TP
.B lk media
Show the active supported media player and track.
.TP
.B lk media toggle
Toggle play/pause, then report the resulting player state and track.
.TP
.B lk media next
Advance to the next track, then report the resulting player state and track.
.TP
.B lk media prev
Return to the previous track, then report the resulting player state and track.
.TP
.B lk media stop
Stop playback, or pause on players without a distinct stop command, then report the resulting state.
.PP
On macOS, LOOK currently controls running Music or Spotify applications.
On Linux, LOOK uses the MPRIS ecosystem through playerctl.
.SH INTELLIGENCE VERSIONS
.TP
.B lk skills version
Show the installed skills schema, bundled skills-pack version, and count of locally learned skills.
.TP
.B lk skills update [FILE]
Refresh the Bundled skills section from LOOK's built-in pack or a compatible external skills file.
The locally Learned section is preserved.
.PP
LO user memory carries a data schema version independent of the LOOK application version.

.SH FAST MEDIA ALIASES
.TP
.B mm
Toggle play/pause.
.TP
.B mn
Advance to the next track.
.TP
.B mp
